        "body": "Symbotic Inc. is a public company headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts, trading under the ticker SYM. SEC records list CIK 0001837240. Its website describes end-to-end warehouse automation solutions for retailers and distributors. The company says its Symbotic Systems combine dense storage, streamlined operations, and AI-enhanced software, and that its Symbotic Solutions can be adapted for palletized goods, small quantity fulfillment, and omnichannel operations. It states that items from 1 lb (0.5 kg) and 2 x 6.4 x 5 in (5.1 x 16.3 x 12.7 cm) up to 60 lb (27.2 kg) and 36 x 24 x 16.2 in (91.4 x 61 x 41.2 cm) can be automatically managed, with cold chain options for loose items.\n\nThe company describes itself as an innovator in robotics and AI for material handling logistics, and says its AI-enhanced software can see beyond warehouse walls. It positions itself as a leader in industrial automation, though this is the company's own characterization. The website text names Symbotic Solutions and Symbotic Systems as its offerings.\n\nMassachusetts public records list 191 legal exposure entries for the company, with no specific cases named in the available data. The company also appears under the alias SYMBOTIC INC.",
